steps=[
 step('Retain the same actual laws, operators and original inputs','Apply the independently accepted actual projected-rotation parent with the six original analytic caller conditions. Extract its same twelve witnesses, actual conditional components and mean preservation. Identify the inherited complete centered and conditional-mean-zero Hilbert spaces explicitly; the typed change only exposes the parent proposition and introduces no assumption.',r'g=U(Pf-(f-Pf)),\quad g_P=A_0f_P-\Gamma_0f_V,\quad g_V=\Gamma_0f_P+A_0f_V.', '  unfold actual_corrector_change_statement','  have hΓself'),
 step('Test the square identity and cancel mixed terms','Positivity gives selfadjoint Γ_0. Test A_0²+Γ_0²=I against u, moving each selfadjoint operator through the inner product, to obtain the norm identity. Move A_0 and Γ_0 through the mixed product and use their commutation to obtain the cross-term identity. These identities hold on the full centered Hilbert space, including the zero space.',r'\|A_0u\|^2+\|\Gamma_0u\|^2=\|u\|^2,\qquad\langle A_0u,\Gamma_0v\rangle=\langle\Gamma_0u,A_0v\rangle.', '  have hΓself','  let K :'),
 step('Derive the corrector operator identities from the same inverse','Set K=A_0 Inv. Evaluate both sides of Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and of the two commutation identities. Consequently KΓ_0=Γ_0K=A_0 and KA_0=A_0K. The inverse remains on H_P^0; it is never extended to constants or assumed to be a new caller certificate.',r'K=A_0\operatorname{Inv},\quad K\Gamma_0=\Gamma_0K=A_0,\quad KA_0=A_0K.', '  let K :','  have hSquareApply'),
 step('Reduce the remaining mixed inner product','Apply A_0²+Γ_0²=I to u. Commutation and KΓ_0=A_0 give A_0 K A_0 u+Γ_0 A_0u=K(A_0²u+Γ_0²u)=Ku. Test against v and use selfadjoint A_0 and Γ_0. This is precisely the mixed term needed for the corrector expansion.',r'A_0KA_0u+\Gamma_0A_0u=Ku,\qquad\langle KA_0u,A_0v\rangle+\langle A_0u,\Gamma_0v\rangle=\langle Ku,v\rangle.', '  have hSquareApply','  have hDiagL'),
 step('Evaluate both diagonal terms and align the mixed terms','Move Γ_0 across the first diagonal inner product, use Γ_0K=A_0, and move A_0 across once more. For the other diagonal use KΓ_0=A_0 directly. Real symmetry and the preceding cross-term identity align the two mixed products without any surjectivity or dimension argument.',r'\langle KA_0u,\Gamma_0u\rangle=\|A_0u\|^2,\quad\langle K\Gamma_0v,A_0v\rangle=\|A_0v\|^2,\quad\langle A_0v,\Gamma_0u\rangle=\langle A_0u,\Gamma_0v\rangle.', '  have hDiagL','  have hCorrector'),
 step('Expand the corrector and compute its exact change','Write X=||A_0u||²,Y=||Γ_0u||²,Z=||A_0v||²,W=||Γ_0v||²,t=⟨A_0u,Γ_0v⟩ and r=⟨Ku,v⟩. For u′=A_0u−Γ_0v and v′=Γ_0u+A_0v, norm expansion gives ||u′||²=X+W−2t and ||v′||²=Y+Z+2t. The diagonal and mixed identities give ⟨Ku′,v′⟩=X−Z+r−2t. Hence C(u′,v′)=(−X−Y+Z+W)/2−r=−||u||²/2+||v||²/2−r. Subtract C(u,v)=(||u||²−||v||²)/2−r. All cross terms cancel and the exact half and signs remain.',r'C(A_0u-\Gamma_0v,\Gamma_0u+A_0v)-C(u,v)=-\|u\|^2+\|v\|^2.', '  have hCorrector','  have hGlobal71'),
 step('Substitute the actual conditional and polar components','For arbitrary actual f with integral zero, use the parent to produce its actual f_P and the actual conditional g_P of the same g. Keep f_V=V_0*Rf and g_V=V_0*Rg. Apply the two-argument congruence of C to the already proved component formulas, then subtract C(f_P,f_V) and apply the preceding algebra with u=f_P,v=f_V. Thus the corrector is evaluated on actual components, rather than components defined by the rotation right-hand sides.',r'f_V=V_0^*Rf,\quad g_V=V_0^*Rg,\quad C(g_P,g_V)-C(f_P,f_V)=-\|f_P\|^2+\|f_V\|^2.', '  have hGlobal71','  have hFinal'),
 step('Reassemble every original clause with the same witnesses','Retain the full-micro intertwining identity, actual projected rotation, pair energy and all earlier law/kernel/root/inverse/polar conclusions, and adjoin only the new corrector identity. This supplies the discrete corrector-change ingredient for the first two signed terms of B4/B28. Time evolution, the weak H1 bridge, nonexplosion, implementation error and expected-cost composition are not inferred from this algebra.',formula, '  have hFinal','\n\nend\n')]
